v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov","html_url":"https://github.com/mekhovov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":1914,"digest":"sha256:82c9751944f469c54ee2ddfcf2cc56fec564691dd29e57d1683f11cde976b3a4","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-09-18T12:00:25Z","updated_at":"2026-09-18T12:00:25Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/releases/download/v0.61.6/verification.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mekhovov/revealline/tarball/v0.61.6","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mekhovov/revealline/zipball/v0.61.6","body":"# v0.61.6 — Versus visible board footprint\n\nThis package records the reviewed Versus visible board footprint source scope below. Its actual qualification and original frozen payload evidence are attached. Affected player journeys and phase acceptance require separate public verification; this package does not claim completion of full-game theme selection, physical-device certification or later phases.\n\nReviewed Versus footprint source scope: per-seat visible board footprint, complete wide and classic arena fitting, intrinsic canvas sizing isolation, resize and content-reflow reconciliation, unchanged-layout geometry read avoidance, cached-page and terminal lifecycle ownership, picture simulation and input identity preservation. Versus visible board footprint: each complete classic or wide board fits its own arena, with painter scaling based on the visible CSS width rather than the element box. Canvas intrinsic dimensions cannot resize the layout. ResizeObserver and the content-change fallback reconcile both settled seats before painting while avoiding unchanged geometry reads. Cached-page restoration refreshes layout without resuming; terminal callbacks cannot resurrect ownership. Simulation, accepted pictures and input identity remain unchanged. The existing logical-pixel actor cap still needs a separate readability decision on narrow boards; this change does not remove it. Historical native evidence remains separately source-scoped; final native and public acceptance remain pending.\n\nExact game source: `4fd8e2dac4fdc851d0d2bf0b21e77162d9d405c9` (tree `d16edac0127fc96139445ae2365cc74499f80921`).\n\nAll six source gates passed through the hosted exact-source workflow. Each of the two complete four-shard families passed 5,865 tests with zero failures, cancellations, skips or TODOs. Production reproduction/readiness and the ordinary build passed on the hosted source. Both hosted source families used Node 20.19.6. No local command gates are claimed by this qualification pipeline; earlier local Versus footprint cohorts remain separately source-scoped corroboration. The full test suite and ordinary build use the actual hosted authority above; no duplicate local execution is claimed.\n\nThe separately authenticated hosted utility inspected the complete frozen original artifact. Its source archive matches all 11,801 tracked files and modes. Every one of the 693 game files matches its original manifest. Local assembly rehashes the retained original metadata and preserves exact runner member descriptors for the source and distribution payloads; it does not download or rehash the large originals locally. The attached evidence preserves the selected original qualification and source-scoped Versus visible board footprint observations, including retained earlier failures; it does not replace verification of this release after deployment.\n\nPredecessor: [v0.61.5](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/releases/tag/v0.61.5). Before selecting or deploying v0.61.6 as current, retain v0.61.5 using its exact immutable published source, distribution and metadata through the capacity-admitted archive process, preserving all earlier catalogue entries and owners. Predecessor source and inspection evidence exist; publication, native/public acceptance and future archive allocation require their own actual authorities. Bind those when available; do not invent a future route or acceptance. Complete the normal main publisher PR/merge, deployed byte verification and applicable native play/offline evidence. Source and attachment qualification alone do not establish public Versus footprint acceptance.\n\nAt package assembly, public byte/play/offline verification is pending; acceptance is recorded separately after publication. Full P03/P05/P07/P08-A/P18 remains incomplete. Modeled input, browser observations and physical-device qualification remain separate evidence categories.\n\n## Later source and release preparation observations\n\nSource PR119 is merged. The exact qualified game source remains `4fd8e2dac4fdc851d0d2bf0b21e77162d9d405c9`; the integration commit preserves later publisher and delivery work. Seven subsequent source-scoped browser cases passed for complete classic/wide boards, the recorded Standard/Large sizes and desktop/portrait/short-landscape navigation. The original pending-native statement above describes package-assembly time. Public v0.61.5 is accepted. Its Archive25 retention deployment is in progress and must pass its own byte and play checks before v0.61.6 becomes current. This draft does not claim public or full P08-A acceptance.\n"}